{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the priest</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other (Ecclesiastes 5:5) וינאץ בזעם אפו מלך וכהן. This is what they said in the chapter \"Makom Shenahagu\" (Yoma 19a): Four cries the Temple courtyard cried out: \"Lift up, your heads, O gates!\" (Psalm 24:7) — and Ishmael ben Phiabi entered and served in the high priesthood; he was righteous, and many ate at his table, and no leftover (notar) was found in his days. And this is וכהן כי יקנה — that he had many acquisitions of persons, therefore it is the beginning of the verse, for he was righteous. But וינאץ בזעם אפו — that is King Yannai, who was wicked; therefore it is the end of the verse. Another interpretation: because there were among them wicked priests who would purchase the priesthood, that which was not theirs — therefore וינאץ בזעם אפו מלך וכהן. <b>בלחמו</b> — three times in the Masorah: here and the others נשחיתה עץ בלחמו (Job 14:7) and [one more occurrence]. Therefore בלחמו preceded נודד (Genesis 4:12) — that they went into exile because of the drawn sword and the bent bow."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The third occurrence of בלחמו is implied by 'ג׳' but the specific citation is not written; the text as given only quotes two explicit occurrences. Also, the final sentence connects בלחמו to Genesis 4:12 נודד תהיה בארץ, though the verse address is not written by the author."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:21.686361539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}